{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-tsx","path":"/blog/2026-05-20--self-hosted-mcp-servers-for-daily-life/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"disqus":"edward-j-schwartz"}},"post":{"htmlAst":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Like many people, when I'm on the go and need to do something, I reach for an LLM\nassistant. In my case, that's Claude. Anthropic, OpenAI, and Google all have\na variety of connections to various services. But what happens when they don't\nhave a connection to a service that you want?"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, I've been dieting, which means I need to track my calories. I\nuse MyFitnessPal for that. Tracking calories is laborious and difficult.\nMuch of the difficulty comes from estimating the calories in a meal. What are\nthe ingredients and components, and how much of each is there? If only there\nwas a way to take a picture and have an intelligent system analyze the image and\ndetermine the calories. Oh wait, we do—LLM assistants!"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sadly, as far as I know, there's no connection to MyFitnessPal in any of\nthe major LLM assistants. Wouldn't it be nice if my LLM could automatically log the\nestimated calories for me after analyzing the image?"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is where self-hosted MCP servers come in. Claude now allows you to add \"custom integrations\" to your account that it can use on the mobile app or on claude.ai. These custom integrations are just SSE-based MCP servers. If you have a server, you can run these integrations yourself."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"There were a few complications for me:"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"ol","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"li","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are several MyFitnessPal MCP servers, but they are "},{"type":"element","tagName":"em","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"stdio"}]},{"type":"text","value":" servers, which do not expose the HTTP endpoints that Claude's custom integrations require."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"li","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Although I have a server, it is behind a firewall, and I don't want to change that."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fortunately, these problems aren't that difficult to solve. For the first\nproblem, I used "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/supercorp-ai/supergateway"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"supergateway"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to\nexpose the stdio MCP server as an SSE MCP server. For the second problem, I used\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://ngrok.com/"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"ngrok"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to create a secure tunnel to my server without\nchanging my firewall settings."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setting up projects like this has never been easier. I asked Claude Code to\nhelp, and it generated "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/edmcman/mcp-servers"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"the "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"docker-compose"}]},{"type":"text","value":" solution"}]},{"type":"text","value":" in about thirty minutes."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"As is becoming more frequent, I found that the existing MyFitnessPal MCP servers\nwere all lacking features I needed, such as the ability to see recent and\nfavorite foods, delete log entries, and so on. So I forked them and vibe-coded\nthe features I wanted.  Forking the MCP servers and customizing them took a couple of hours spread over a few days of testing. Coding agents make this type of project easier than\never."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I'm still working out some edge cases with meal recognition and calorie estimation accuracy, but I've been really happy with the core functionality. Here's a screenshot of Claude estimating calories for some fries I photographed and logging them to MyFitnessPal automatically:"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[]},{"type":"element","tagName":"figure","properties":{"className":["gatsby-resp-image-figure"],"style":""},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n    "},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"className":["gatsby-resp-image-wrapper"],"style":"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 1534px; "},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n      "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"className":["gatsby-resp-image-link"],"href":"/static/1e09ad3276320909df12aa40eb25e562/ddc6c/image.png","style":"display: block","target":"_blank","rel":["noopener"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n    "},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"className":["gatsby-resp-image-background-image"],"style":"padding-bottom: 75.77777777777777%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;"},"children":[]},{"type":"text","value":"\n  "},{"type":"element","tagName":"picture","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n          "},{"type":"element","tagName":"source","properties":{"srcSet":["/static/1e09ad3276320909df12aa40eb25e562/e46ac/image.avif 450w","/static/1e09ad3276320909df12aa40eb25e562/9b8d4/image.avif 900w","/static/1e09ad3276320909df12aa40eb25e562/95aab/image.avif 1534w"],"sizes":"(max-width: 1534px) 100vw, 1534px","type":"image/avif"},"children":[]},{"type":"element","tagName":"source","properties":{"srcSet":["/static/1e09ad3276320909df12aa40eb25e562/8626f/image.webp 450w","/static/1e09ad3276320909df12aa40eb25e562/131f1/image.webp 900w","/static/1e09ad3276320909df12aa40eb25e562/611a4/image.webp 1534w"],"sizes":"(max-width: 1534px) 100vw, 1534px","type":"image/webp"},"children":[]},{"type":"text","value":"\n          "},{"type":"element","tagName":"source","properties":{"srcSet":["/static/1e09ad3276320909df12aa40eb25e562/fc2a6/image.png 450w","/static/1e09ad3276320909df12aa40eb25e562/1cfc2/image.png 900w","/static/1e09ad3276320909df12aa40eb25e562/ddc6c/image.png 1534w"],"sizes":"(max-width: 1534px) 100vw, 1534px","type":"image/png"},"children":[]},{"type":"text","value":"\n          "},{"type":"element","tagName":"img","properties":{"className":["gatsby-resp-image-image"],"src":"/static/1e09ad3276320909df12aa40eb25e562/ddc6c/image.png","alt":"Screenshot of using MyFitnessPal integration in Claude","title":"","loading":"lazy","decoding":"async","style":"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;"},"children":[]},{"type":"text","value":"\n        "}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n  "}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n    "}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n    "},{"type":"element","tagName":"figcaption","properties":{"className":["gatsby-resp-image-figcaption"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Screenshot of using MyFitnessPal integration in Claude"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n  "}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In claude.ai, I've created a project and been using memory to teach Claude about my diet, which is fortunately quite repetitive."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check out the "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/edmcman/mcp-servers"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"docker-compose setup and MyFitnessPal MCP server fork on GitHub"}]},{"type":"text","value":". The MyFitnessPal MCP server is included as a submodule."}]}],"data":{"quirksMode":false}},"excerpt":"Like many people, when I'm on the go and need to do something, I reach for an LLM\nassistant. In my case, that's Claude. Anthropic, OpenAI…","timeToRead":2,"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2026-05-20--self-hosted-mcp-servers-for-daily-life/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["ai","llm","project"],"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","bio":"Computer Security Researcher","twitter":"@edmcman","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/4ed6d/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/4ed6d/ed.png 80w","sizes":"80px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/1deab/ed.webp 80w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"80px"}]},"width":80,"height":80}}}},"title":"Self-hosted MCP Servers for Daily Life","updatedDate":"May 20, 2026","image":null}},"recents":{"edges":[{"node":{"id":"82e49e36-8948-598b-be15-e61c2e3146e5","fields":{